{"title":"Mock AIME 6 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_6_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the coordinate plane, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20ae344d73db0349b15012d38c5b8f4e4b0dee55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_k(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> rotation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> around the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895a7206b880989aa9ab15210abce1b1b4d984c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2000-k,k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b56b0a2ee5528a759b7def1ee792ce2d2e7da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2007,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546e1ed0040263eace269f0a29b70451d56f31f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+1}=T_n(P_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/9238d82d59d5dfe79e96d916bfdf2f4acc4ed3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/49945f5f2646906d60085f52046827d417ddec25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b7d819d135d04c5c51f0475f0397919e908b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$433$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_6_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f74b7b36cc295349c0c4e19b1dc7993d3419d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> be the rotational matrix for a point to rotate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b953d396f434900925523b4e79b2ff52346e40a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> around the origin:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1055c0477ec47f026ff8b5684c966277b2470fc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(\\theta)=\\begin{bmatrix} cos(\\theta) &amp; -sin(\\theta)\\\\ sin(\\theta) &amp; cos(\\theta) \\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"210\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/67227c5501c8a0fcefd2a2acd2c0a370a5cb8583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef70378ea993d0ffd9f1df6df6697d47e8cd210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=\\begin{bmatrix} cos(90^\\circ) &amp; -sin(90^\\circ)\\\\ sin(90^\\circ) &amp; cos(90^\\circ) \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 0 &amp; -1\\\\ 1 &amp; 0 \\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"313\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e07421af7c7522c9883c3f0e032b57831c859d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> be the point of rotation, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c1f0129b04dffff628721abd3703e86e9fb852a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_r=\\begin{bmatrix} 2000-n \\\\ n \\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"133\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Let's write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> in matrix form as: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e21370251dfaa4dd246ec5c46567a506b5e0e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n=\\begin{bmatrix} P_{x_n} \\\\ P_{y_n} \\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"94\" height=\"45\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/368585a507265a9fdd547764acbda5292b48c63c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{x_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c7561ae63f04b51ffb8982fd93d6fa4de03f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" /> are the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>We can write the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c898e4838db56320e10a77c62839f4237c974733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> by translating the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> to the origin, multiply it by the rotation matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and then add the point subtracted:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f930c5c642857d9cd3e2a4dcc0b93102f6ef158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+1}=(R)(P_n-P_r)+P_r=\\begin{bmatrix} 0 &amp; -1\\\\ 1 &amp; 0 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} P_{x_n}-(2000-n) \\\\ P_{y_n}-n \\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix} 2000-n \\\\ n \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2000-P_{y_n} \\\\ P_{x_n}+2n-2000 \\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"739\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Now we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba01f7f3fe30dc94dad1276948a71927034d8ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/981eadcd9f5947ebb33fcd7588fd039b9715aec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+2}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2000-P_{y_{n+1}} \\\\ P_{x_{n+1}}+2n-2000 \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2000-(P_{x_n}+2n-2000) \\\\ (2000-P_{y_n})+2(n+1)-2000 \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 4000-P_{x_n}-2n \\\\ -P_{y_n}+2(n+1) \\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"687\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>For this problem, we're only interested in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate.  So,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae981981b4fb6c480674bd9055fa04ee18a3f7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{n+1}}=P_{x_n}+2n-2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"197\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14fd7c71b1a7909b5bc9cd076a9dcc8c6cdd911c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{n+2}}=-P_{y_n}+2(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"197\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b978c97eb4eeb70a1a36b021ea1fc6431e766b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(n+1) \\equiv 0\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17ce24f793b342f4d3d72890a6311d9e25dbb722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{n+2}} \\equiv P_{y_n}\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe0d0b7b416e6d7ba605ccfda6450c055b01dac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_0}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> and we're looking at a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b7d819d135d04c5c51f0475f0397919e908b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$433$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7bec728da938cec32c7be189f35b5a9078f29078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$433 \\equiv 1\\; (mod\\;2) \\not\\equiv P_{y_0}\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"248\" height=\"20\" />.  \n</p><p>Therefore we need to calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/3743e9cb43fa76e90154feadb52ee7b91a733e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"28\" height=\"19\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a0f70642fc76d4a2fde103b79f3901adad5fe26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_1}=P_{x_0}+(2)(0)-2000=2007-2000=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"358\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/2686d421685627663f66a4d17107637f58a77d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_m} \\equiv 1\\; (mod\\;2)\\equiv P_{y_1}\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"251\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>So, we use the recursive formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd0ff919685620b6e4e13d097f881c6ec40f003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{n+2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/3743e9cb43fa76e90154feadb52ee7b91a733e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"28\" height=\"19\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a4a4c900eb0611d6f259deb60311b46c138b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_3}=-P_{y_1}+(2)(1)+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58f6c7e05dad6db2809339ef48a1557ca63b0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_5}=-P_{y_3}+(2)(3)+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cb30b0889df67235e8c51b337388aac572daaaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_7}=-P_{y_5}+(2)(5)+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>and we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceafaea2cecbbc9f1c94aac00f3fb2d749e8190a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{2q+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f2d7b969a8501fd112a43076e2156b2ee07ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd07c22f181e6e0a63b6133f5914ec20f1d03299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{2q+1}}=-P_{y_{2q-1}}+2(2q-1)+2=-P_{y_{2q-1}}+4q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"383\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a687d085a548305d790124d010d2e93b7c8d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{2q+1}}=(-1)^q P_{y_1}+4(q-(q-1)+(q-2)-(q-3)+....+0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"499\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da4658805dca9c3cf89d27fb9552fc49f6882edc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{2q+1}}=(-1)^q P_{y_1}+4 \\left( \\begin{cases} q, &amp; q\\;is\\;odd \\\\ 0, &amp; q\\;is\\;even\\end{cases}+\\begin{cases} -\\frac{q-1}{2}, &amp; q\\;is\\;odd \\\\ \\frac{q}{2}, &amp; q\\;is\\;even\\end{cases} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"495\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780e618b711b6da80e43e4df3853c007591ca5f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{2q+1}}=(-1)^q P_{y_1}+ \\begin{cases} 2q+2, &amp; k\\;is\\;odd \\\\ 2q, &amp; q\\;is\\;even\\end{cases}=(-1)^q P_{y_1}+ 2q+\\begin{cases} 2, &amp; q\\;is\\;odd \\\\ 0, &amp; q\\;is\\;even\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"597\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ceb3c3efa421c86f027971e006dcef2049cab8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{2q+1}}=(-1)^qP_{y_1}+2q+(1-(-1)^q)=(-1)^q(P_{y_1}-1)+2q+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"506\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1e53beb8d890c16974e75a1b27f43368d5c3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{2q+1}}=433$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fffc2a713708f6d3966079a5967192688b3cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_1}=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> then we solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c685d2db3f29489bb7ec0ce8e148ea35edf0ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^q(7-1)+2q+1=433$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"224\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a649fe3b177e7cc58c46eaa1bc82d9eec2a7b03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=\\frac{433-1-(-1)^q6}{2}=216-(-1)^q3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"301\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82845e36a0bb450a339095b8e36f92908e6b460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm 1 \\equiv 1\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a52c335a576f92a85d88489ed9c81338ac30cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm 3 \\equiv 1\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bd6d3a30817d358006886c9a7a5fb9ff3fc7874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^q3 \\equiv 1\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02ef3bd2d2e883c0a1b3bf5d2744739e844f2e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(216-(-1)^q3) \\equiv 1\\; (mod\\;2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is odd.\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/76264ad457a9776fe1ca65757576c90f79c7736e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=216-(-1)(3)=219$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5852e555c7256a4538b99cc8b485f70a89e168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2q+1=(2)(219)+1=\\boxed{439}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"274\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_6_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040545\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 243/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 386/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13943/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.381      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.381      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25881:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040545 and revision id 205783. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}